    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195-a4">

                <pb facs="0351" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg289"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 13.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Liddell to Mr. Hoppin</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Home Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-09-07"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 7,
                        1878</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Private.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: As the time is approaching for the
                    liberation of the two Fenian convicts at Portland and their transmission to
                    America, Mr. Cross desires me to ascertain whether any arrangements have been
                    made by their friends or Mr. Welsh as to providing them with a passage and
                    outfit; for those matters will have now to be attended to, as the pardons will
                    be ready before very long.</p>
                <p>I am, dear sir, truly yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item>A. F. LIDDELL.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Hoppin</hi>, Esq.</item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
